=A prospect replied positively and isn't out-of-office. *Reply to them yourself.*

Lead: {{ $json.payload.lead_email }}
Campaign: {{ $json.payload.campaign_id }}
Their reply: "{{ $json.payload.reply_text }}"

Automated voice is OUT OF SCOPE — no call is placed by this system, by anyone, ever, on the current design. Approve = you are taking the follow-up; Decline = not a real lead, and it is logged. Nothing here dials, reveals a phone number, or spends a credit.

parameters.jsCode:
// Turn one classified inbound Instantly event into the facts the three Sheet writes need.
//
// Runs for EVERY authenticated event, not only the ones that reach a human. That is the whole
// point: before this existed, a reply was classified, posted to Slack and then died — nothing
// recorded that the lead replied, and an opt-out that only reached Slack would still be contacted
// on LinkedIn, because the Suppression tab never heard about it.
//
// Input  = the Leads tab, from "Read Leads (reply lookup)" (one empty {} placeholder item when the
//          tab holds only its header row — alwaysOutputData).
// Also reads "Dedup + TCPA Gate" for the payload + the OpenAI sentiment it already parsed.
//
// OPT-OUT IS DECIDED FROM PHRASES, NOT FROM SENTIMENT. "Not interested, we already have a vendor"
// is negative but is NOT a request to stop; "please take me off your list" is friendly and IS one.
// Sentiment is recorded on the lead row, never used to suppress.
// Erring toward suppressing is the only safe direction in a compliance check (same doctrine as
// VIO-intake-verify-curate's blank-identifier_type rule), so an out-of-office that still contains
// an explicit opt-out phrase DOES suppress — an OOO on its own never does.
const OPT_OUT_PATTERNS = [
  /\bunsubscrib/,
  /\bopt(?:ing)?[\s-]*out\b/,
  /\bopt\s+(?:me|us)\s+out\b/,
  /\bremove\s+(?:me|us|my|our|this)\b/,
  /\btake\s+(?:me|us)\s+off\b/,
  /\bstop\s+(?:emailing|e-mailing|mailing|contacting|messaging|reaching|sending)/,
  /\bdo\s*n(?:o|')?t\s+(?:email|e-mail|contact|message)\s+(?:me|us)/,
  /\bno\s+longer\s+(?:wish|want)\s+to\s+(?:receive|hear)/,
  /\bdelete\s+(?:my|our)\s+(?:email|e-mail|address|data|details|information|info|contact)/
];

const stripHtml = (s) => String(s === null || s === undefined ? '' : s).replace(/<[^>]*>/g, ' ');
const norm = (s) => stripHtml(s).replace(/[‘’]/g, "'").replace(/\s+/g, ' ').toLowerCase().trim();
const EMAIL_RE = /^[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+$/;
const firstEmail = (vals) => {
  for (const v of vals) {
    const e = String(v === null || v === undefined ? '' : v).trim().toLowerCase();
    if (e && EMAIL_RE.test(e)) return e;
  }
  return '';
};
const str = (v) => String(v === null || v === undefined ? '' : v).trim();

const leadRows = $input.all()
  .map((i) => (i && i.json) || {})
  .filter((r) => r && typeof r === 'object' && Object.keys(r).length > 0);

const out = [];
for (const it of $('Dedup + TCPA Gate').all()) {
  const g = (it && it.json) || {};
  const p = (g && g.payload) || {};
  const s = (g && g.sentiment) || {};
  const eventType = str(p.event_type).toLowerCase();

  const isBounce = /bounce/.test(eventType) || p.bounced === true || str(p.status).toLowerCase() === 'bounced';
  const isUnsubEvent = /unsub/.test(eventType) || p.unsubscribed === true || p.is_unsubscribe === true;
  const isReply = /repl/.test(eventType);

  // Opens, clicks and sends change no reply/bounce state — there is nothing to record for them.
  if (!isReply && !isBounce && !isUnsubEvent) continue;
  // A replay the gate already rejected must not double-write (Suppression is append-only, so a
  // duplicate there is harmless but noisy; a duplicate Events row would overstate the OpenAI spend).
  if (g.decision === 'skip' && /duplicate/i.test(str(g.reason))) continue;

  const text = norm([p.reply_subject, p.subject, p.reply_text, p.reply_text_snippet, p.reply_html,
    p.text, p.body, p.message].filter((v) => v !== null && v !== undefined).join(' \n '));
  let phraseHit = '';
  for (const rx of OPT_OUT_PATTERNS) {
    try { if (rx.test(text)) { phraseHit = String(rx); break; } } catch (e) { /* never throw on a weird payload */ }
  }

  const optOut = isUnsubEvent || Boolean(phraseHit);
  const suppress = optOut || isBounce;
  const suppressionReason = optOut ? 'opt_out' : (isBounce ? 'bounced' : '');

  // Instantly's reply/bounce payloads name the prospect `lead_email`; the rest are defensive
  // fallbacks for shapes seen on other events. `from_email` is last because on anything other than
  // an inbound reply it can be OUR sending account, and suppressing ourselves would be a bad day.
  const email = firstEmail([p.lead_email, p.contact_email, (p.lead || {}).email, p.prospect_email,
    p.email, p.from_email, p.from_address]);

  const payloadLeadId = str(p.lead_id) || str(p.leadId);
  let row = null, matchOn = '', matchValue = '';
  if (payloadLeadId) {
    row = leadRows.find((r) => str(r.lead_id) === payloadLeadId) || null;
    if (row) { matchOn = 'lead_id'; matchValue = payloadLeadId; }
  }
  if (!row && email) {
    row = leadRows.find((r) => str(r.contact_email).toLowerCase() === email) || null;
    if (row) { matchOn = 'contact_email'; matchValue = str(row.contact_email); }
  }

  const sentiment = str(s.sentiment).toLowerCase() || 'unknown';
  const ooo = s.out_of_office === true;
  const now = new Date().toISOString();

  // A bounce is NOT a reply: it must never overwrite reply_received / reply_sentiment on the row.
  let leadUpdate;
  if (isReply) {
    leadUpdate = { reply_received: true, reply_sentiment: sentiment, reply_out_of_office: ooo, updated_at: now };
  } else if (isBounce) {
    leadUpdate = { channel_state_email: 'bounced', updated_at: now };
  } else {
    leadUpdate = { updated_at: now };
  }

  const parts = [];
  if (isReply) parts.push('reply ' + sentiment + (ooo ? ' (out-of-office)' : ''));
  if (isBounce) parts.push('bounce');
  if (isUnsubEvent && !isReply) parts.push('unsubscribe event');
  parts.push(suppress ? ('suppressed: ' + suppressionReason) : 'not suppressed');
  if (suppress && !email) parts.push('NO EMAIL IN PAYLOAD - suppression row NOT written, add it by hand');
  parts.push(matchOn ? ('Leads row matched on ' + matchOn) : 'no Leads row matched');

  out.push({ json: {
    event_type: eventType || '(missing)',
    decision: str(g.decision),
    is_reply: isReply,
    is_bounce: isBounce,
    is_unsubscribe_event: isUnsubEvent,
    opt_out: optOut,
    opt_out_match: phraseHit,
    suppress: suppress,
    suppression_reason: suppressionReason,
    suppression_identifier: suppress ? email : '',
    reply_sentiment: sentiment,
    reply_out_of_office: ooo,
    lead_email: email,
    lead_id: payloadLeadId || str((row || {}).lead_id),
    source_config: str((row || {}).source_config) || str(p.source_config),
    match_on: matchOn,
    match_value: matchValue,
    lead_update: leadUpdate,
    event_result: parts.join(' - '),
    timestamp: now
  }});
}
return out;

// Only a lead we actually LOCATED on the Leads tab is updated, and only ever by the column that
// matched it — lead_id here, contact_email in the sibling node. Returning [] stops the branch, so
// an unmatched event writes nothing rather than updating the wrong row.
//
// Keys below MUST equal Leads column names: the Sheets node runs in autoMapInputData mode and
// matches on header TEXT. The live column order does NOT match SHEET_SCHEMA.md (lead_id is column
// P), so nothing here may address a column by its A1 letter. Routing fields are dropped on purpose
// so the item handed to the Sheets node contains real columns only.
return $input.all()
  .map((i) => (i && i.json) || {})
  .filter((o) => o.match_on === 'lead_id' && o.match_value)
  .map((o) => ({ json: Object.assign({ lead_id: o.match_value }, o.lead_update || {}) }));

// Fallback path: the event carried no lead_id, or its lead_id is not on the Leads tab, but the
// prospect's address is. Same rules as the sibling node — header-name matching only, real columns
// only, [] when there is nothing to update.
return $input.all()
  .map((i) => (i && i.json) || {})
  .filter((o) => o.match_on === 'contact_email' && o.match_value)
  .map((o) => ({ json: Object.assign({ contact_email: o.match_value }, o.lead_update || {}) }));

// APPEND-ONLY. Never update, never delete a Suppression row: a suppression added in error is
// corrected by ADDING a row that notes the correction (SHEET_SCHEMA.md).
//
// A row is written only when there is a real address to put in identifier_value. A blank value
// would be compared against every identifier shape by VIO-intake-verify-curate's suppression
// check — a blank/unrecognised row is deliberately matched against everything there — so writing
// one could block the whole pipeline. When the payload carried no address the Events row says so
// in plain words instead, for a human to fix by hand.
const seen = [];
return $input.all()
  .map((i) => (i && i.json) || {})
  .filter((o) => o.suppress === true && o.suppression_identifier && o.suppression_reason)
  .filter((o) => {
    const k = o.suppression_identifier + '|' + o.suppression_reason;
    if (seen.indexOf(k) !== -1) return false;
    seen.push(k);
    return true;
  })
  .map((o) => ({ json: {
    identifier_type: 'email',
    identifier_value: o.suppression_identifier,
    reason: o.suppression_reason,
    added_at: o.timestamp,
    added_by: 'VIO-inbound-reply-to-call'
  }}));

// One Events row per classified inbound event. Keys MUST equal Events column names.
//
// tool/action are `openai` / `classify_reply` because that is what actually happened and what
// actually cost money: the OpenAI Classify node sits BEFORE the gate, so it runs on every
// authenticated event — a bounce costs a classification too. `units: 1` is the honest meterable
// fact (one chat completion).
//
// est_cost_usd is left blank on purpose: measure, don't estimate. A made-up number in the cost
// meter is worse than a gap — fill it from real OpenAI usage, not from a guess.
return $input.all().map((i) => (i && i.json) || {}).map((o) => ({ json: {
  timestamp: o.timestamp || new Date().toISOString(),
  lead_id: o.lead_id || '',
  lead_email: o.lead_email || '',
  tool: 'openai',
  action: 'classify_reply',
  units: 1,
  est_cost_usd: '',
  result: o.event_result || '',
  workflow: 'VIO-inbound-reply-to-call',
  source_config: o.source_config || ''
}}));
